  <revision rev="1" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>a768142ee9683b7d24f444766d9a2bac</srcmd5>
    <version>1.0+git20260112.dcbc9c0</version>
    <time>1794236900</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>- Initial submission of tela (test execution framework with dynamic
  hardware/system resource matching and TAP13 reporting).
- Developed by IBM Linux on Z for automated hardware qualification
  (DASD, QETH, APQN, CPACF, and virtualization).
- Tested and builds cleanly across all architectures (s390x, x86_64,
  aarch64, ppc64le).
- License: MIT (verified).
- Includes tela-test subpackage with upstream test suite and a verified,
  non-destructive s390x sample test archive.
- Already reviewed and accepted in devel:tools.
- Fix Factory Auto review error &quot;Source URLs are not valid&quot;:
  * Set Source0 to %{name}-%{version}.tar.gz as the git snapshot archive
    is generated via _service (tar_scm) from commit dcbc9c0, avoiding
    404 download errors during automated source verification.
</comment>
    <requestid>1396334</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="2" vrev="2">
    <srcmd5>7aeac64782bc4b34c449b3b93aa87129</srcmd5>
    <version>1.0+git20260112.dcbc9c0</version>
    <time>1794838494</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>- Implement hypervisor profiles in tela-s390x-tests.tar.gz:
  * Add .telarc and telastate profiles for bare-metal LPAR, z/VM,
    and KVM hypervisors (telarc.lpar, telastate.lpar, telarc.zvm,
    telastate.zvm, telarc.kvm, telastate.kvm).
  * Add dedicated non-destructive test cases for z/VM (test_zvm_guest.sh:
    CP query, minidisk, Virt.NIC QDIO, CHPIDs) and KVM (test_kvm_guest.sh:
    vCPUs, VirtIO SCSI CCW, firmware IPL facilities).
  * Enhance run_tests.sh to support hypervisor selection in mock,
    match, tap, and live modes (e.g. ./run_tests.sh mock all).
  * Update s390x-tests/README.md and USER-GUIDE.md with multi-hypervisor
    testing instructions.
</comment>
    <requestid>1397898</requestid>
  </revision>
</revisionlist>
